      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOVELA (2) brings the most convincing profile, having finished fourth in a 3yo+ Class 6 at Cairns when beaten a length and a half after leading deep into the straight. His prior BM65 third also reads well for this, and the record at 1200m with Lauren Guernier back aboard gives him a sound winning case despite the distance query. STOKOMO (5) is the obvious danger after missing by a nose in a BM70 at Townsville, with his consistency over the past 12 months offsetting the fact he is still winless at the trip. ASK ME MATE (1) has been kept fresh, won an easy Townsville trial and drops back from a Class 5 over 1400m, but he was a beaten favourite last start and carries 61kg. BANCORY BAY (4) has a genuine place hope if his Townsville sixth is treated leniently after home-turn interference, though being unplaced from five goes at 1200m keeps him behind the main pair.",
